          "settings": {
            "heading": "Autumn 2024 Press Release",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "alignment": "left"
          }
        },
        "text_QFk6Tx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>New York City - 03 October 2024 </strong></span><em><strong> - Hartwick Atelier Unveils Debut Collections in New York: A New Era of Limited Edition Slow Fashion</strong></em></p><ul><li><em>Specializing in Handspun and Handwoven Fabrics, Natural Dye Silks, and Handcrafted Fine Jewellery</em></li><li><em>Sophisticated Lifestyle Collections, Made by Master of Heritage Craft</em></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.hartwickatelier.com/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Hartwick Atelier</span></a>, an emerging innovator in limited edition slow fashion, is thrilled to announce the launch of its debut collection of apparel, fine silk, and fine jewellery.</p><p>Hartwick Atelier is a fresh arrival on the slow fashion scene, presenting a euro chic ready-to-wear collection in finely-tailored artisanal fabrics and a handcrafted jewellery line that dazzles with hand-carved precious stones and fine gold.</p><p>Founder and Creative Director Angela Hartwick’s elegant lifestyle collection brings together the work of masters in Indian heritage craft with her years working as a stylist and filmmaker in Paris, Dubai and Mumbai. Showcasing the analogue beauty of handspun and handwoven fabrics, hand block prints, natural dyes, fine tailoring, and handcarved precious gems – each handcrafted piece in her collection is a glimpse into the rich history and intricate process that has gone into its creation. </p><p>The scope of the collection is a reflection of its founder’s own lifestyle, a spectacular and fascinating blend of cultures, elegance and earthiness. Her ethos comes together in this luscious offering with authentic range. </p><p>True to form, Hartwick Atelier’s launch is unfolding in a series of salon-style evenings along the path of Hartwick’s travels this fall, starting in Tatlayoko Lake, Canada where she and her photographer husband have hand built their off-grid homestead deep in pristine wilderness. Moderated, invite-only events in New York, Paris and Dubai will lead to a month-long boutique residency on Chiltern Street in London in December [a collaboration with longtime friend Mickey Ashmore, founder of the iconic handcrafted <a href=\"https://uk.sabah.am/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Sabah Shoes</span></a> brand.]</p><p><em>“The intention is to invite people into a conversation about true sustainability in fashion, to create an opportunity to really see and feel the fabrics, and to foster an appreciation for the mastery in these pieces…”</em></p><p><em>“This collection came together over decades of world travel as creatives in fashion and film. At first glance, it’s an elegant lifestyle brand with a distinct character and gorgeous texture. But at its roots, this collection is a portrait of nature and sustainability through refined handcraft. It’s an analogue love story\", says Angela Hartwick, Founder and Creative Director. </em></p><p>Click <a href=\"https://www.hartwickatelier.com/pop-ups\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">here</span></a> for an invitation to our New York Press Event on October 17, 2024</p>",
            "text_size": "text-std",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_indent": "noindent"
          }
        }
